1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Commercial Purpose" means any use intended for or resulting in economic gain, or any use by, for, or on behalf of a for-profit entity, including:

(a) Use by any for-profit organization, company, partnership, sole proprietorship, business, commercial entity, or any organization operated for profit, whether for business operations, internal workflows, customer-facing services, evaluation, testing, benchmarking, trial, development, or any other purpose.

(b) Use for internal business operations, including data processing, reporting, automation, decision-making, or other activities supporting core functions or commercial operations.

(c) Use by any individual while acting within the scope of their employment, using employer-provided equipment, or performing duties on behalf of a for-profit organization, regardless of when or where the code was written or created.

(d) For the avoidance of doubt: use of the Software by a for-profit organization for evaluation, testing, benchmarking, trial, proof-of-concept, or non-production purposes is a Commercial Purpose and is strictly prohibited without a separate commercial license granted through prior paper Written Consent.

(e) Use in connection with commercialized education, paid education, fee-based education, corporate training, paid workshops, bootcamps, tutoring, offline education, in-person education, or any educational activity that is not a Permitted Educational Use.

(f) Inclusion, combination, linking, bundling, or distribution of the Software with or within any Commercial-Related Bundle, even if that bundle is provided free of charge, even if no direct fee is charged, and even if the third-party components in that bundle are licensed under terms that permit commercial use.

Non-profit organizations may use the Software only as expressly permitted by this license, only if they are legally recognized as non-profit, and only if they do not use the Software to generate revenue, provide fee-based services, or further any Commercial Purpose. For-profit entities are strictly prohibited from all use.

1.2 "Modified Version" means any version differing from the original source code release, including:

(a) Changes to source code files.

(b) Addition, removal, or modification of files or directories.

(c) Changes to configuration files affecting Software behavior, except as permitted in Section 2(e).

For clarity, changes to configuration files that consist solely of parameter or setting changes and contain no source code, scripts, executable logic, or other code do NOT constitute a Modified Version, whether or not they are publicly shared in accordance with Section 2(e).

For the avoidance of doubt: Packaging unmodified Software alongside other software on the same medium does NOT constitute a Modified Version, provided source files remain unchanged and the Software is not recompiled or altered. However, any distribution, publication, sharing, uploading, transmission, or making available of the Software or any Modified Version to any third party requires prior paper Written Consent, except as expressly allowed by this license. Transfer of the Software or its Modified Versions between different departments, subsidiaries, affiliates, friends, colleagues, students, research collaborators, or any other third parties constitutes distribution and is strictly prohibited without prior paper Written Consent, except as expressly allowed by Section 1.4 and Section 2(e).

1.3 "Permitted Educational Use" means use solely in a publicly available, free-of-charge course on a mainstream online platform, where:

(a) The course is open to the public on a mainstream online platform.

(b) The course is free of charge. No payment, subscription, paid enrollment, paid certificate, mandatory paid membership, or other mandatory fee is required to access the course content.

(c) The course is not commercialized education, not corporate training, not fee-based education, not a paid workshop, not a bootcamp, not paid tutoring, not offline education, not in-person education, and not part of any for-profit educational program.

(d) The Software is not distributed, uploaded, shared, sublicensed, sold, or made available to students or any third party. Students and participants must obtain the Software only from the Project Owner's official channels.

(e) Any use of the Software in the course remains non-commercial and does not generate revenue, directly or indirectly, for any person or entity.

(f) For the avoidance of doubt, a mainstream online platform itself shall NOT be deemed a Commercial-Related Bundle solely because the platform is operated by a for-profit entity, provided that: the course is free of charge; the course has no advertising, no paid promotion, no paid membership requirement, and no commercial sponsorship related to the Software; and the Software itself is not distributed through the course. If any of these conditions is not met, the exception in this Section 1.3(f) does not apply.

All other educational use is prohibited. Without limitation, offline education, in-person teaching, school or university offline classes, paid online courses, paid platforms, paid training, corporate learning, and commercial educational services are strictly prohibited.

1.4 "Permitted Research Use" means non-commercial academic, scholarly, or personal research use by an individual or a legally recognized non-profit organization, provided that:

(a) The research is not intended for or resulting in economic gain.

(b) The research is not performed for or on behalf of a for-profit entity.

(c) Subject to the conditions below, research collaboration is permitted, including:

    (i) online non-public collaboration through private channels;

    (ii) offline, non-public, face-to-face collaboration;

    (iii) sharing necessary research results, data, reports, drafts, and materials among direct research collaborators;

    (iv) peer review, including providing confidential materials to reviewers;

    (v) publication of papers, preprints, reports, results, and data, provided that no source code, Modified Version, binary, or material allowing reconstruction of the Software is included or made available without prior paper Written Consent.

(d) Direct research collaborators may exchange files, including Modified Versions or source code solely for Permitted Research Use, only if all of the following conditions are met:

    (i) the exchange is offline, non-public, or through a private non-public online channel;

    (ii) each collaborator has independently obtained the Software from the Project Owner's official channels, or the exchange is strictly necessary for the research and not for redistribution;

    (iii) the exchanged material is not uploaded to any public repository, public platform, preprint server, package manager, container registry, cloud storage, messaging group, or any other public or semi-public location;

    (iv) the exchanged material is not used for any Commercial Purpose;

    (v) the exchanged material is not further distributed to any person who is not a direct research collaborator;

    (vi) each recipient remains bound by this license;

    (vii) this license is retained in full with any exchanged copy.

(e) Online non-public collaboration is permitted, including private meetings, private emails, private file transfers, and private repository access limited to direct research collaborators, provided that no public upload, public repository, public preprint, public package, public container, or public distribution of the Software, Modified Version, source code, or binary occurs.

(f) Peer review is permitted. A researcher may provide the Software, Modified Version, source code, binary, data, results, or reports to a reviewer solely for confidential peer review, provided that the reviewer is bound by confidentiality, does not use the material for any Commercial Purpose, does not distribute it further, and does not publish it. The reviewer must destroy or return all copies after review unless retention is required by law or journal policy, in which case the reviewer remains bound by this license.

(g) Publication of papers, preprints, reports, results, and data is permitted, provided that no source code, Modified Version, binary, or material allowing reconstruction of the Software is included or made publicly available without prior paper Written Consent. Publication of results and data does not grant any right to use the Software commercially.

