    (iii) Permitted Research Use;

    (iv) internal administrative use by a legally recognized non-profit organization, but only using the original, unmodified Software, and only if the organization does not generate revenue and does not provide fee-based services.

(b) Modify the source code solely for Your own personal, private use, or for Permitted Research Use as expressly allowed by Section 1.4. Modified Versions are for personal or Permitted Research Use ONLY and may NOT be distributed, published, shared, uploaded, transmitted, given, lent, transferred, sublicensed, sold, or made available to any third party, except as expressly allowed by Section 1.4. Non-profit organizations may not modify the source code for internal administrative use.

(c) Submit contributions (Pull Requests). By doing so, you agree:

    (i) You retain copyright of your contribution.

    (ii) You grant the Project Owner (KUSSA/KUSSA_LTSC) a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable, sublicensable license to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, and monetize your contribution.

    (iii) The Project Owner has sole authority to determine commercial licensing, distribution, and monetization terms.

    (iv) Your contribution will only be accepted if both you AND the Project Owner agree to its inclusion. You represent that you have read, understood, and voluntarily agree to these terms.

(d) You may NOT distribute, publish, share, upload, transmit, lend, give, or make available the Software or any copy, whether original or modified, to any third party without prior paper Written Consent, except as expressly allowed by Section 1.4 and Section 2(e). If paper Written Consent is granted for original unmodified copies, distribution must be non-commercial, must include this license intact, and must comply with all restrictions in this license.

(e) Modify configuration files or settings solely to enable or change operational parameters for Your own permitted use. Such modifications do NOT constitute a Modified Version, provided source files remain unchanged and the configuration file contains no source code, scripts, executable logic, or other code.

You MAY publicly share, publish, upload, or distribute such configuration files, and any person may do so, subject only to the following conditions:

    (i) the configuration file must not contain, embed, or reproduce any source code, Modified Version, binary, executable code, script, or any material that would allow reconstruction of the Software;

    (ii) the configuration file must not be represented as official, approved, or supported by the Project Owner;

    (iii) this license should be included in full with the public configuration, or a prominent link to this license should be provided alongside it;

    (iv) the public configuration must not be used to train, fine-tune, distill, evaluate, benchmark, or otherwise develop any AI or machine learning model.

Public sharing of configuration files under this Section 2(e) is permitted even on public code hosting platforms, provided the Software itself, its source code, any Modified Version, and any binary are not uploaded or made available in the same public repository, gist, package, or distribution. This permission does not grant any right to publish the Software or any Modified Version.

(f) Private Storage: You may make necessary backups, temporary copies, private CI/CD runs, private containerization, and private cloud deployments solely for personal private use, non-profit internal administrative use of the original unmodified Software, Permitted Educational Use, or Permitted Research Use, provided that:

    (i) no copy is made available to any third party, except as expressly allowed by Section 1.4;

    (ii) no copy is public;

    (iii) no copy is used for any Commercial Purpose;

    (iv) no copy is used to train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise develop any AI model;

    (v) this license is retained in full;

    (vi) private repositories remain private and are not forked to public repositories.

For the avoidance of doubt, using a for-profit platform for Private Storage, private CI/CD, private containers, or private cloud does not by itself constitute a Commercial-Related Bundle or a violation of Section 3(h), provided the conditions in this Section 2(f) are met.

(g) No other permissions are granted. All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Project Owner.

